# NOTE: playletra.com is currently served as plain static files from a
# Railway service, which does NOT read this file. It is kept because it
# is correct for Cloudflare Pages or Netlify if hosting ever moves, and
# because it documents the intended routing. What actually makes
# /privacy, /terms and /hello work today is the host resolving an
# extensionless path to the matching .html file. /go works because
# public/go.html is a real file.
#
# Static pages that live outside the React app. These sit above the
# SPA catch-all because the first matching rule wins.
/privacy    /privacy.html    200
/terms      /terms.html      200
/hello      /hello.html      200

# Countable entry point for ads and bios: lands on the parent-facing
# landing with a source tag that the visit ping forwards. No cookie,
# no identifier — just a word in the query string.
/go         /?src=ad         302

# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback. Every path that isn't a real file in
# the build (e.g. /play, /play/spell-word, /play/find-alphabet, the
# /dev/* tools) needs to serve index.html so the React app can read
# location.pathname and route accordingly. Without this Cloudflare
# returns a 404 for any URL except / and the asset paths.
#
# /api/* never reaches this file: public/_routes.json sends those to
# the Pages Functions in functions/api/ first.
/*    /index.html    200
